-- title:
--   Determinant-shell integral over a twisted centralizer at a division place
-- statement:
--   Let $K$ and $L$ be number fields with $L$ a $K$-algebra of degree $2$, let $\sigma$ be a $K$-automorphism of $L$ such that every $K$-automorphism of $L$ lies in the subgroup generated by $\sigma$, let $v$ be a nonzero prime of $\mathcal{O}_K$ and $c$ a unit of the completion $K_v$. Let $\delta\in\mathrm{GL}_2(L\otimes_K K_v)$ satisfy `IsNormOf`, i.e. there is $y$ with the base-change image of the scalar matrix $c$ equal to $y^{-1}\cdot\mathrm{normString}(\sigma,\delta)\cdot y$, and assume $\delta$ is $\sigma$-conjugate to no scalar: for every unit $z$ of $L\otimes_K K_v$ there is no $x$ with $\mathrm{scalar}(z)=x^{-1}\,\delta\,\sigma_{\mathrm{GL}}(x)$, where $\sigma_{\mathrm{GL}}$ is $\sigma\otimes\mathrm{id}$ on matrices. Write $T=\{t: t\,\delta\,\sigma_{\mathrm{GL}}(t)^{-1}=\delta\}$ for the twisted centralizer, with its Borel structure, and for $n\in\mathbb{N}$ let $\mathrm{Sh}_n\subseteq T$ be the set of $t$ whose determinant is the image under $\mathbb{1}\otimes-$ of some $s\in K_v^\times$ with $|s|_v=\exp(-n)$. Let $\tau'$ be a Haar measure on $T$, let $t_v\in[0,\infty]$ satisfy $\tau'(\mathrm{Sh}_0)\cdot N(v)=t_v+\tau'(\mathrm{Sh}_0)$ with $N(v)$ the absolute norm of $v$, let $r<1$ in $[0,\infty]$, and let $F:T\to[0,\infty]$ take the value $r^n$ on $\mathrm{Sh}_n$ for every $n$. Then both $\int_{\bigcup_n \mathrm{Sh}_n}F\,d\tau'$ and $\sum_{n\ge 0} r^n\,\tau'(\mathrm{Sh}_n)$ equal $t_v\,(N(v)-1)^{-1}(1-r)^{-1}$.
--
--   This is the evaluation of the local zeta integral over the twisted centralizer at a place where the relevant quaternion algebra ramifies, the determinant shells $\mathrm{Sh}_n$ playing the role of the valuation filtration on reduced norms. It feeds the computation of the norm-weighted orbital integral over such a centralizer, which in turn supplies one Euler factor in the comparison of twisted orbital integrals.
